# Uniform kinetic and viscous ledger for the velocity-endpoint Galerkin family

The physical velocity endpoint generates every canonical finite Galerkin
orbit.  Its `ℓ²` norm pays the complete finite initial kinetic square,
uniformly in the internally generated radius.  The exact finite kinetic
identity then pays both the later kinetic energy and the integrated
vorticity mass on every prefix of `[0,1]`.

No energy budget, radius, cutoff, branch, or target trajectory is accepted by
the source-facing producer.
-/

